      "marks": 4,
      "answer": "$x=-1-\\sqrt5i$ and $x=\\frac32$.",
      "official_mark_scheme_text": "State second root $-1-\\sqrt5i$ — B1.\n\nCarry out a complete method for finding a quadratic factor with zeros $-1+\\sqrt5i$ and $-1-\\sqrt5i$ — M1.\n\nObtain $x^2+2x+6$ — A1.\n\nObtain root $x=\\frac32$ — A1. Guidance: OE.\n\nAlternative 1: state second root $-1-\\sqrt5i$ — B1; $(x+1-\\sqrt5i)(x+1+\\sqrt5i)(2x+a)=2x^3+x^2+6x-18$ — M1; $(1-\\sqrt5i)(1+\\sqrt5i)a=-18$ — A1; $6a=-18$, $a=-3$, leading to $x=\\frac32$ — A1 OE.\n\nAlternative 2: state second root $-1-\\sqrt5i$ — B1; POR $=6$, SOR $=-2$ — M1; obtain $x^2+2x+6$ — A1; obtain $x=\\frac32$ — A1 OE.\n\nAlternative 3: state second root $-1-\\sqrt5i$ — B1; POR $(-1-\\sqrt5i)(-1+\\sqrt5i)a=9$ — M1 A1; obtain $x=\\frac32$ — A1 OE.\n\nAlternative 4: state second root $-1-\\sqrt5i$ — B1; SOR $(-1-\\sqrt5i)+(-1+\\sqrt5i)+a=-\\frac12$ — M1 A1; obtain $x=\\frac32$ — A1 OE.\n\nPrinted total: 4.",
